{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D12","page":1,"quote":"⌀ 16 H7 (+0.018/0)"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT)"}],"comment":"The ⌀16 H7 hole (D12) is a tight-tolerance fit feature, but the drawing does not account for the I.Z.B.P. plating thickness specified in the title block. Plating buildup will reduce the bore diameter and can cause interference with the mating shaft; the designer must either increase the pre-plate bore size or add a note masking the hole during plating."
    ,
    "recommended_correction":"Increase the bore dimension to allow for plating thickness, or specify that the hole is to be masked during I.Z.B.P. plating."}]}
